# Repositories hack/verify-multiarch.sh lets stay single-arch in a release.
# One repository per line, no tag or digest, each with a `# reason`: why the
# image cannot be built for both architectures, not that it has not been yet.
#
# A leading `*/` matches that image under any registry and owner, by the tail
# of its path. A first-party image is published wherever the build was told to
# publish it -- upstream's own registry, or a fork's -- so an entry naming one
# registry excuses it there and nowhere else, and the same tree built elsewhere
# sees the same image refused.
*/e2e-sandbox  # CI harness only, an x86 KVM sandbox (packages/core/testing pins linux/amd64); never runs on a user cluster
